{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":326,"code_snippet":"if [[ \"$RED_EXIT\" -eq 126 || \"$RED_EXIT\" -eq 127 ]]; then … finish NOT_A_RED 4","finding":"A test file absent at the red commit yields VERIFIED on the prescribed invocation (no --test-file): sh/python exit 2 and pytest exit 4 with file-not-found output are accepted as assertion failures.","reasoning_trace":"Read the red-side gate at :322-337 and NOT_A_RED_PATTERNS at :52-71; neither covers exit 2/4 or 'cannot open'/'No such file'. Built a fixture whose red commit predates the test; `--red <pre-test> -- sh tests/test_add.sh` printed 'sh: 0: cannot open tests/test_add.sh' and 'verdict: VERIFIED', exit 0. Both prescribed invocations (micro-sprint.md:43, reviewing-code/SKILL.md:219) omit --test-file.","critique":"The classifier accepts any non-0/126/127 exit as 'failed by assertion'.","remediation":"Add file-not-found shapes to NOT_A_RED_PATTERNS; gate sh/python exit 2 and pytest exit 4 when the output names a missing path; make --test-file mandatory in the prescribed invocations; add a default-path bats case expecting exit 4.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-754 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":227,"code_snippet":"ln -s \"${MAIN}/${d}\" \"${wt}/${d}\"","finding":"Linked dependency directories (node_modules .venv vendor target .tox) make both runs resolve the live tree's source through workspace links or editable installs, so uncommitted state decides the verdict despite the header promise at :27.","reasoning_trace":"link_deps symlinks $MAIN/<dir> into each worktree by default. Fixture: node_modules/pkg -> ../src/pkg in the live tree, red commit with failing test + buggy src, green commit with no fix, fix only as an uncommitted edit. Result: red exit 0, green exit 0, 'verdict: DECOY' exit 3 although green holds no fix.","critique":"Source resolution through the link is not covered by the documented write-through caveat.","remediation":"Make linking opt-in or refuse to link a directory that resolves back into $MAIN (.pth/__editable__ scan for venvs; symlink entries resolving outside node_modules); add a workspace-link bats case; amend the header.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-706 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/706.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/skills/reviewing-code/SKILL.md","line":6,"code_snippet":"Bash(.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh *)","finding":"The review role (deny_raw_shell: true) gains a wildcard grant on a script that execs the argv after -- verbatim (red-test-check.sh:250) and a second argv from --setup; the test command is taken from engineer-authored reviewer.md.","reasoning_trace":"Compared base and head allowed-tools and capabilities.execute_commands (:27 args: [\"*\"]). Read run_bounded: exec \"$@\" with cwd in a worktree, full env and uid. Reproduced `-- bash -c '…'` running in both worktrees. SKILL.md:219 instructs taking the red commit and test command from reviewer.md.","critique":"A single * grant on an argv runner removes the fence that keeps the review gate near read-only.","remediation":"Runner-specific allowlist patterns; drop --setup from the review grant; refuse inline-code interpreters and network fetchers as argv[0] unless --allow-shell; print the resolved argv in the verdict.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-269 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/269.html","CWE-78 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html","OWASP ASVS V1.4 https://owasp.org/www-project-application-security-verification-standard/"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":227,"code_snippet":"ln -s \"${MAIN}/${d}\" \"${wt}/${d}\"","finding":"Engineer-controlled red/green commits can write through the linked dependency symlinks into the operator's live node_modules/.venv/vendor/target/.tox; the writes persist after the worktrees are removed.","reasoning_trace":"Fixture: red-commit test wrote node_modules/.bin/jest; after the run the live file contained 'planted'. --no-link-deps is opt-out and SKILL.md:219 does not prescribe it. Audit dissent DISS-C-002.","critique":"Documented at :29-30 but the safe mode is not the default.","remediation":"Opt-in linking, read-only copies, or a --no-link-deps instruction in the review skill.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-61 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/61.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":250,"code_snippet":"( cd \"$cwd\" && unset GIT_DIR GIT_WORK_TREE GIT_INDEX_FILE GIT_PREFIX && exec \"$@\" )","finding":"The test argv inherits the reviewer's full environment (provider keys, GitHub token) and the output tails are printed and emitted as red_tail/green_tail for the reviewer to cite into tracked files.","reasoning_trace":"Only GIT_* are unset. Reproduced: AUDIT_PROBE_SECRET=sk-test-1234 … -- sh -c 'echo leak=$AUDIT_PROBE_SECRET' printed the value in both tails. Audit dissent DISS-C-003.","critique":"Inherent to any runner, aggravated by the role boundary and the artifact copy.","remediation":"env -i with an allowlist or unset known credential names; pass tails through pii-filter.sh.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-526 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/526.html","CWE-200 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/red-test-check.sh","line":275,"code_snippet":"kill \"$WATCH_PID\" 2>/dev/null || true","finding":"In the no-timeout/gtimeout path the watcher is killed mid-sleep after the direct child dies, so its KILL never lands and TERM-ignoring grandchildren survive the run and the cleanup.","reasoning_trace":"wait \"$RUN_PID\" at :270 returns on the direct child; RUN_PID cleared at :273; watcher killed at :275 during the 2 s sleep at :260. The review reproduced two orphaned sleep processes; confirmed by reading.","critique":"RTC-8/9 use TERM-honouring sleep and cannot see it.","remediation":"wait on the watcher when the timed-out flag is set; signal the recorded process group in cleanup; add a TERM-ignoring child to RTC-9.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-404 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/404.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/validate-artifact.sh","line":1297,"code_snippet":"n = gsub(/[.!?]+[)\"]*[[:space:]]/, \"&\", s)","finding":"Abbreviations (e.g., i.e., etc.) count as sentence ends; a legitimate two-sentence definition is rejected with exit 1 by a validator CI runs on both glossaries.","reasoning_trace":"Reproduced: '**Eg**: A sample, e.g. this one. Another sentence here.' -> 'has 3 sentences; at most two', exit 1.","critique":"Fail-closed heuristic without an abbreviation allowance.","remediation":"Skip boundaries after e.g./i.e./etc./vs./cf., or require an uppercase/digit next character.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-185 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/185.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"reliability","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/tools/check-glossary-terms.sh","line":82,"code_snippet":"if (t ~ /^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$/ && !(t in seen))","finding":"Only single-token spans are kept, so the gate resolves 0 kernel tokens to a definition (5 alias, 11 allowlisted) while the workflow header claims every backticked framework term resolves to an entry or alias.","reasoning_trace":"Ran the head script against the workspace kernel: 'kept: 16; defined: 0; alias: 5; allowlisted: 11; missing: 0'. Allowlist admits 'full' and 'ultra'.","critique":"Contract overstates reach.","remediation":"Keep two- or three-word spans, or restate the header as a single-token drift check.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1068 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
